 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? That' frustrating. Do you walk long way, or take a bus that gets stuck in the same place? Then walking it in advance is your best insurance. A clear path from door to the bus stop means you not waiting in the cold for ages. Then the local bus company often keeps a pool of vehicles with snow tires or chains, and sends them out. Bring a warm drink, warm socks and something to read. Sitting still in a warm bus is often better than an hour outside in the cold.",
